{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH4Semisimple","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeH4Semisimple","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH4Wedderburn","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MatrixSemisimple"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H4.exists_pairing_ne_zero₄","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H4.exists_pairing_ne_zero₄","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH4Semisimple.lean#L116-L686","doc":"**Trace nondegeneracy of the level-4 Markov pairing (sorry-free)** —\nthe rank-4 analogue of `HeckeH3GramNondegeneracy.exists_pairing_ne_zero`,\nproved **det-free** (audit route (ii)): whenever the five per-block\nMarkov weights are nonzero, every nonzero `y` pairs nontrivially with\nsome `w` under `trM4`.  The witness is the `wedderburnInvV₄` preimage of\nthe dual elementary matrix in a block where `y`'s image is nonzero.\nThis is the trace-nondegeneracy half of the Wenzl hypothesis pair at\nthe 3→4 tower rung — what a future genuine `WenzlTowerStep` instance\nconsumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H4.trM4_eq_blocks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H4.trM4_eq_blocks","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH4Semisimple.lean#L91-L113","doc":"**The Wedderburn block decomposition of the level-4 Markov trace\n(sorry-free):** `trM4 = Σ_λ y_λ·χ_λ` with the five explicit weights —\n24 scalar identities rolled into one linear goal, closed by\n`linear_combination` against `mul_inv_cancel₀` with sympy-derived,\nexactly-verified cofactors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H4.markovWeight211","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H4.markovWeight211","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH4Semisimple.lean#L85-L87","doc":"Markov weight of the $(2,1,1)$ block weight; numerator $q^2(z-q)(qz+1)(q^2 z - (q^3 - z))$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H4.markovWeight31","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H4.markovWeight31","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH4Semisimple.lean#L81-L83","doc":"Markov weight of the $(3,1)$ block weight; numerator $-q(z-q)(qz+1)((q^2+1)qz+1)$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H4.markovWeight22","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H4.markovWeight22","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH4Semisimple.lean#L77-L79","doc":"Markov weight of the $(2,2)$ block weight; numerator $-q^3(z-q)(qz+1)$ — the rank-3 degeneracy pair $(z-q)$, $(qz+1)$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H4.markovWeightMinus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H4.markovWeightMinus","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH4Semisimple.lean#L73-L75","doc":"Markov weight of the $(1,1,1,1)$ (sign) character weight; numerator $-q^3(z-q)(q^2 z - (q^3 - z))((q^4+q^2)z - (q^5 - z))$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H4.markovWeightPlus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H4.markovWeightPlus","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH4Semisimple.lean#L69-L71","doc":"Markov weight of the $(4)$ (trivial) character weight; numerator $(qz+1)((q^2+1)qz+1)((q^4+q^2+1)qz+1)$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H4.isSemisimpleRing_H4A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H4.isSemisimpleRing_H4A","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH4Semisimple.lean#L55-L62","doc":"**H₄(q) is a semisimple ring at every Wenzl-generic parameter\n(sorry-free):** transfer along the explicit rank-4 Wedderburn\nisomorphism, with the matrix factors supplied by\n`QOU.MathlibExt.MatrixSemisimple`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}